%% alt: Cache-aside, read then write. Read: the app asks the cache, gets a miss, reads the database, and stores the value with a TTL. Write: the app updates the database first, then deletes the cache entry.
%% caption: On a write, the database changes first, and the cache entry is deleted rather than overwritten.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant App as App server
  participant Cache
  participant DB as Database
  rect rgba(254, 243, 199, 0.45)
  Note over App,DB: Read
  App->>Cache: get user:42
  Cache-->>App: miss
  App->>DB: read user 42
  DB-->>App: row
  App->>Cache: set user:42 with TTL 300 s
  end
  rect rgba(237, 233, 254, 0.45)
  Note over App,DB: Write
  App->>DB: update user 42
  DB-->>App: ok
  App->>Cache: delete user:42
  end
